ggml-zendnn: GGML_ZENDNN_ALLOW_MUL_MAT_ID, and it proved the decline moot

MUL_MAT_ID was declined when a MoE run aborted, and that decline predates 86d0937,
which gave GGML per-group INT8 a per-expert matmul_direct route. This switch lifts
it so the question can be settled rather than argued, and also counts the decline
as a rejection instead of returning silently -- several older paths in this
function return false without touching the counters, which is how "accepted but
never executed" looked like a mystery for weeks.

The answer is that the decline was not what was stopping it. With the switch on,
qwen3-coder-30b-a3b dispatches exactly the same ops as with it off -- 5376 q4_K
and 802 q6_K either way, identical in every column. The gate that refuses it is
max_experts = 32 against this model's 128, and the line after would refuse it too:
N/n_experts <= 32, where MoE decode routes about eight active rows across 128
experts.

That is not a bug to widen. gather+matmul+scatter needs enough rows per expert to
amortise a per-expert GEMM, and a 128-expert model in decode gives it a fraction
of one. See docs/perf/moe_expert_dispatch_a10.csv.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-zendnn/ggml-zendnn.cpp	2026-08-17 13:47:23.756733067 +0000
+++ ggml/src/ggml-zendnn/ggml-zendnn.cpp	2026-08-17 13:47:23.780286276 +0000
@@ -948,7 +948,22 @@
                     // qwen3-coder-30b-a3b killed llama-bench with signal 6 that
                     // way. Accepting an op the library cannot serve is worse
                     // than declining it, so decline.
-                    if (op->op == GGML_OP_MUL_MAT_ID) {
+                    // GGML_ZENDNN_ALLOW_MUL_MAT_ID=1 lifts this to find out
+                    // whether it is still true. The decline was added when a
+                    // MUL_MAT_ID reached AOCL-DLP and aborted, BEFORE
+                    // group_matmul gained a per-expert matmul_direct route for
+                    // GGML per-group INT8 on non-VNNI hosts. The backend already
+                    // slices the weight per expert -- batch_wei is
+                    // src0->data + cur_a*nb02 -- so the shape reaching the
+                    // library is 2-D and may now be expressible.
+                    static const bool allow_mmid = [] {
+                        const char *e = std::getenv("GGML_ZENDNN_ALLOW_MUL_MAT_ID");
+                        return e != nullptr && std::atoi(e) != 0;
+                    }();
+                    if (op->op == GGML_OP_MUL_MAT_ID && !allow_mmid) {
+                        if (zendnn_dispatch_stats::enabled()) {
+                            g_zendnn_stats.rejected[weights->type]++;
+                        }
                         return false;
                     }
                     // Only the quantised types this fork actually has kernels
